{"type":"message","id":"7c70ddf8","parentId":"83c22305","timestamp":"2026-04-08T12:49:57.735Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"790\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"sender\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-04-08 12:49 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Matteo Cicalese (495506013)\",\n  \"id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"name\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"username\": \"CicaMatt\"\n}\n```\n\ntest the slm-expert skill with this input and tell me what returnw:\n\"In a synthetic case, a 58-year-old with long-standing hypertension has creatinine 1.7 mg/dL, urine albumin-creatinine ratio 420 mg/g, and persistent blood pressure around 158/96 despite amlodipine. What kidney-related complications and treatment priorities should be considered?\""}],"timestamp":1775652597732}}
